================================================================================
PENDING ATTRIBUTION OBLIGATIONS
================================================================================

The following are known obligations to resolve BEFORE the first public
release. They are tracked here so they are not forgotten:

1. Icon set (@jitoffice/icons)
   All icons are drawn from scratch for this project. No third-party icon
   fonts or icon packages may be bundled: a compiled font binary silently
   merges the licenses of its individual glyphs and the per-glyph license
   files are typically dropped at build time, which breaks the attribution
   chain irrecoverably.
   Status: no icons implemented yet.

2. Emoji / symbol assets
   Not bundled. Symbol insertion renders Unicode text via the user's font
   stack. If graphic emoji are ever introduced, note that OpenMoji is
   CC-BY-SA-4.0 (incompatible), and Twemoji assets are CC-BY-4.0
   (attribution required even though its code is MIT).
   Status: policy set, no assets.

3. Fonts
   Only OFL-1.1 / Apache-2.0 families may be bundled, and only as an opt-in
   package (@jitoffice/tokens/fonts). Candidate families: Inter,
   Noto Sans SC, Noto Sans JP, Source Han Sans, Source Han Serif,
   JetBrains Mono, Sarasa Gothic.
   "PingFang SC", "Microsoft YaHei" / "微软雅黑", "Yu Gothic" and
   "Hiragino Kaku Gothic ProN" may appear ONLY as local-name fallbacks in
   font-family strings. Referencing a family name is not redistribution;
   packaging the font file is.
   Sarasa Gothic's license must be re-verified at every release.
   Status: no fonts bundled.

4. Default theme derived from JitWord / JitKnow UI
   The default design tokens are seeded from values observed at runtime on
   https://jitword.com and https://know.jitword.com (see
   prd/01-design-tokens.md, section 0).
   Imitating a visual style is not infringement; shipping exported assets
   from a design file IS a derivative work. Written confirmation of rights /
   assignment from the design owner must be obtained and archived under
   docs/legal/ before the default theme is published.
   Status: OUTSTANDING — blocking for first release.

5. Documentation and demo content
   Screenshots, sample documents, and preset templates must not contain real
   company names, third-party trademarks, or recognizable Microsoft Office
   interface elements. Microsoft Office's icons, fonts, and interface
   elements are protected by Microsoft trademark and copyright.
   Status: no content yet.

6. Design research sources
   prd/ documents cite observable facts about Element Plus, Arco Design Vue,
   Naive UI, TDesign Vue Next, Ant Design Vue, Vant, and DevUI — package
   metadata, license fields, build scripts, and published dist output. These
   are referenced for comparison and no source code has been copied from
   them. All are MIT-licensed, which would permit copying with attribution
   under the rules at the top of this file should that become necessary.
   Status: reference only, no code incorporated.
